From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: ROG5 at least 8 bpc on native DP sinks, warn on a link too small for the mode

With msm.dpu_mode_clk_check=halved (0139) GNOME offered the MSI MPG 491C
3840x1080@144 (666.25 MHz) and 5120x1440@100 (805.12 MHz) and set both:

  DP: 3840x1080@144 pclk 666250 kHz, 4 lanes x 540000 kHz, bpp 24
  DP: 5120x1440@100 pclk 805120 kHz, 4 lanes x 540000 kHz, bpp 18
  [dpu error]enc37 frame done timeout (x3, during 5120x1440@100)

The halved clock rule is not what let 5120x1440@100 through. These limits
apply to a mode that wide, compared with stock msm-5.4 (lahaina) and the
hardware; the DP bridge and dpu_crtc_mode_valid() check the first three,
the atomic check the rest:

- DPU core clock: two layer mixers behind 3D merge each take half the
  pixels. Stock's sde_kms_get_mixer_count requires htotal * vtotal *
  vrefresh * 1.05 / num_lm to fit the max MDP clock (460 MHz), i.e. pclk
  <= ~876 MHz with two mixers. The halved rule matches this. 5120x1440@60
  (469 MHz) ran at 460 MHz with no underrun (0118 logs none). 0099 still
  votes the full pixel clock, clamped to 460 MHz.
- DP stream clock: stock qcom,max-pclk-frequency-khz = 675000, checked at
  pclk / 2 with the wide bus (dp_display_validate_pixel_clock), the same
  as mainline's DP_MAX_PIXEL_CLK_KHZ check. The PHY's divided VCO clock is
  1350 MHz at HBR/HBR2/HBR3. Above 337.5 MHz the pixel clock needs MMCX
  NOM (stock dispcc-lahaina rate_max). Mainline's DP OPP table (link clock
  only) votes NOM only at HBR3; the DPU's 460 MHz OPP (NOM) covers it, and
  0099 votes that OPP for every mode clock above ~440 MHz.
- Link: 4 lanes x HBR2 (0138 caps HBR3 unless msm.dp_hbr3=1) carry
  17.28 Gbit/s. 5120x1440@100 needs 19.3 Gbit/s at 24 bpp and fits only
  at 18 bpp. dp_min_bpc (0134) defaulted to mainline's 6 bpc floor, so the
  mode was offered and a 10 bpc OLED was driven at 6 bpc.
- SSPP, multirect, resources and memory bandwidth: plane and CRTC atomic
  checks (rect clock <= max core clock, max_linewidth 4096, parallel
  multirect of two linear 2560-pixel rects allowed as stock). The mode
  size is limited to 2 x 2560 by 4096.

Default dp_min_bpc to 8 so that a mode which fits the link only below 8 bpc
is rejected (MODE_BAD). A sink that asks for less (EDID bpc, downstream
port) still gets its own depth, and msm.dp_min_bpc=6 restores mainline's
fallback. This is policy: 5120x1440@100 was the only mode with frame done
timeouts, but that does not show 6 bpc caused them (18 bpp filled 84 % of
the link). With halved (the default since r110, 0139) the MSI list
becomes 1920x1080@60/120, 2560x1440@60/120, 3840x1080@60/100/144 and
5120x1440@60. With
msm.dp_hbr3=1, 5120x1440@100 is offered again at 30 bpp (93 % of 4 x HBR3;
each mixer needs 423 MHz). It is within the stock limits but untested.

3840x1080@144 stays. At 24 bpp it uses 92.5 % of 4 x HBR2 (0145 trains
4 x HBR2 with its 95 % margin). The stream clock is 333 MHz, each mixer
needs 350 MHz of 460, and each SSPP rect less than that. The ASUS stock
refresh cap is 144 Hz. It ran for 20 s without underrun or frame done
timeout, which shows brief operation, not sustained. It cannot run at
30 bpp over HBR2.

Mode validation and bpp selection assume the maximum link, but training
can end on a smaller link (msm's downshifts, including 0145's fallback to
the maximum link, or msm.dp_max_rate), and nothing reports it; the
inherited retry loop can even end with rc 0. Warn when the final link
carries less than the mode needs. The patch also
documents the halved budget and its dependence on the 0099 vote in
dpu_crtc_mode_valid(). Found by GPT-6.1-Sol's review, not fixed here:
TU/blanking feasibility is not a mode validation limit, and 420-only
modes pick bpp with clock/2 at validation but the full clock at modeset.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
index f70c655..19b8b97 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -1768,6 +1768,19 @@ static enum drm_mode_status dpu_crtc_mode_valid(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 	 * SM8350 underran on every frame (blue: 1-2 % or no clock margin).
 	 * msm.dpu_mode_clk_check=halved (the default) restores the halving;
 	 * full keeps this rule.
+	 *
+	 * The halved budget is stock msm-5.4's (sde_kms_get_mixer_count, from
+	 * htotal * vtotal * vrefresh): each of the two layer mixers behind 3D
+	 * merge takes half the pixels, so pclk * 1.05 / 2 must fit the max core
+	 * clock (pixel clocks up to ~876 MHz at 460 MHz; 5120x1440@60 at
+	 * 469 MHz ran without underruns). Other limits: the DP bridge checks the
+	 * stream clock (DP_MAX_PIXEL_CLK_KHZ at pclk / 2 with the wide bus,
+	 * 675 MHz as stock) and the link at the dp_min_bpc floor (0147, 0138's
+	 * HBR2 cap); the atomic check covers the SSPP rect clock, line width,
+	 * multirect, resources and bandwidth; the size check is below. The 0099
+	 * vote stays at the full pixel clock: its 460 MHz OPP also keeps MMCX
+	 * at NOM, which the DP pixel clock needs above 337.5 MHz (stock
+	 * dispcc-lahaina), i.e. for mode clocks above 675 MHz.
 	 */
 	if (READ_ONCE(dpu_mode_clk_check) == DPU_MODE_CLK_CHECK_HALVED &&
 	    dpu_kms->catalog->caps->has_3d_merge &&
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
index 9d01632..0931283 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -2651,6 +2651,19 @@ int msm_dp_ctrl_on_link(struct msm_dp_ctrl *msm_dp_ctrl)
 	if (ctrl->link->sink_request & DP_TEST_LINK_PHY_TEST_PATTERN)
 		return rc;
 
+	/*
+	 * ROG5: mode validation and bpp selection assume the maximum link, but
+	 * msm's downshifts (and dp_max_rate) can end training below what the
+	 * mode needs, and nothing reports it. Say so (0147).
+	 */
+	if (!rc && need_kbps &&
+	    !msm_dp_ctrl_link_carries(ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes,
+				      ctrl->link->link_params.rate, need_kbps, 100))
+		drm_warn(ctrl->drm_dev,
+			 "DP: link %u lanes x %u kHz carries less than the mode's %llu kbit/s\n",
+			 ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes,
+			 ctrl->link->link_params.rate, need_kbps);
+
 	if (rc == 0) {  /* link train successfully */
 		/*
 		 * do not stop train pattern here
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
index 17deb74..eab405e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
@@ -323,10 +323,16 @@ static void msm_dp_panel_cap_pcon_rate(struct msm_dp_panel *msm_dp_panel,
  * (6 = mainline). A DP-to-HDMI/DVI converter always gets at least 8: HDMI and
  * DVI have no 6 bpc (stock msm-5.4 forces 24 bpp for HDMI bridges too,
  * dp_asus_validate_24_bpp). Modes that fit only below the floor are rejected.
+ *
+ * Default 8: with 6, the MSI MPG 491C (10 bpc OLED) was offered 5120x1440@100
+ * (805 MHz), which fits 4 x HBR2 only at 18 bpp; GNOME listed it, set it and
+ * the DPU logged frame done timeouts (2026-09-30). A monitor is never meant to
+ * be driven at 6 bpc when it did not ask for it: a sink whose own ceiling
+ * (EDID bpc, downstream port) is below 8 still gets its depth, see below.
  */
-static uint msm_dp_min_bpc = 6;
+static uint msm_dp_min_bpc = 8;
 module_param_named(dp_min_bpc, msm_dp_min_bpc, uint, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(dp_min_bpc, "ROG5: min bits per component for native DP sinks, 6 or 8 (converters: always 8)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dp_min_bpc, "ROG5: min bits per component for native DP sinks, 8 (default) or 6 (mainline); converters: always 8");
 
 static u32 msm_dp_panel_get_supported_bpp(struct msm_dp_panel *msm_dp_panel,
 		u32 mode_edid_bpp, u32 mode_pclk_khz)
